  , modifyAssistantRequestTemperature :: !(Maybe Double) -- ^ "temperature" - What sampling temperature to use, between 0 and 2. Higher values like 0.8 will make the output more random, while lower values like 0.2 will make it more focused and deterministic. 
  , modifyAssistantRequestTopP :: !(Maybe Double) -- ^ "top_p" - An alternative to sampling with temperature, called nucleus sampling, where the model considers the results of the tokens with top_p probability mass. So 0.1 means only the tokens comprising the top 10% probability mass are considered.  We generally recommend altering this or temperature but not both. 
